1. Introduction
1.1 Purpose
Guidance: State the purpose of this SRS and the software product it describes (name and version). Identify the intended readers.
This document specifies the software requirements for [Product Name], version [x.x]. It is intended for [developers, testers, project guide, end users].
1.2 Document Conventions
Guidance: Explain naming, numbering and priority conventions used in this document.
* Functional requirements are labelled FR-xx, non-functional requirements NFR-xx, use cases UC-xx, interface requirements IR-xx.
* Priority levels: High (must have), Medium (should have), Low (nice to have).
* The words shall (mandatory), should (recommended) and may (optional) are used as defined in IEEE standards.
